;; A descriptor database carrying a construct this generator CANNOT express, so
;; the canary can prove the refusal fires rather than being approximated.
;;
;; `holder.nested` names an enum that is not in the database. That is not a
;; contrived shape: the parser that produces a real database reads enums at FILE
;; level only, so an enum declared INSIDE a message is dropped while the fields
;; referring to it survive with a reference that resolves to nothing. A map
;; field lands in the same place, because the entry message is dropped too.
;;
;; An emitter that guessed here would write a type name nothing declares, and
;; the failure would surface at the consumer rather than at generation.
{:messages
 {"pgbad.Holder"
  {:id "pgbad.Holder"
   :name "Holder"
   :package "pgbad"
   :source "none"
   :fields [{:number 1 :name "nested" :type :enum :type-ref "pgbad.Holder.Nested"}
            {:number 2 :name "ok" :type :bool}]}}
 :enums {}}
